# PCDEMOS/relic - what does not belong in the repository
#
# Two different reasons live in this file and they are not the same
# weight. The first block is a LEGAL boundary; the rest is housekeeping.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The 1998 release itself. NOT REDISTRIBUTED.
#
# CLAUDE.md's legal note: this is a personal interoperability and
# preservation effort, and the original executable and data file are not
# redistributed. Notes and reconstructed source are our own work product
# and those ARE committed.
#
#   reverse/ghidra/relic, relic.dat   the originals
#   reverse/extracted/                every byte of it, carved out of
#                                     relic.dat by datlist.py
#   reverse/patched/                  the MEMF-cleared copy, which is the
#                                     original with seven bytes changed
#
# All of it regenerates from files the user already has:
#   py -3.10 tools/dat/datlist.py --extract reverse/extracted
#   py -3.10 tools/hunk/hunk_memf_any.py reverse/ghidra/relic \
#                                        reverse/patched/relic_anymem
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
reverse/ghidra/
reverse/extracted/
reverse/patched/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Ghidra project database.
#
# Covered by reverse/ghidra/ above; repeated by pattern so a project
# moved to another directory stays ignored. ~16 MB that rebuilds from an
# import, plus per-machine lock files and scratch .ps files Ghidra leaves
# inside the .rep.
#
# NOTE: the database is NOT a build artifact - it holds every name, type
# and comment this project has produced, and nothing else is a copy of it
# (CLAUDE.md rule 6.4). It is excluded because it is large and binary,
# not because it is disposable. reverse/exports/ is the committed,
# diffable projection of it and IS tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*.gpr
*.rep/
*.lock
*.lock~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The MCP server list.
#
# It names one machine's layout - an interpreter, a bridge script that
# lives outside this repository - so it cannot be shared.
# .mcp.json.example is the tracked copy, with every path replaced by a
# <placeholder>; copy it and fill them in.
#
# NO PORT IS PINNED IN EITHER. Three Ghidra projects can share a machine
# and the port a given one answers on depends on which started first, so
# a pin fails by connecting to the WRONG DATABASE rather than by
# erroring. CLAUDE.md 2.1.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.mcp.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local tool state and scratch
#
# Rule 14 puts scratch files in %TEMP%, so these are a backstop for the
# times that slips rather than an expected location.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json
*.png
*.ppm
*.bin
!tools/**/*.py

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS droppings
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# C build output. The sources under src/ are tracked; nothing a
# compiler makes from them is.
build/
out/
*.obj
*.exe
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.lib
*.suo
*.user
.vs/
CMakeFiles/
CMakeCache.txt

# NOT the project files - src/relic.sln and the two .vcxproj are
# HAND WRITTEN and tracked. There is no CMake here: MSVC is the
# Windows build and tools/build_web.sh is the emscripten one, and
# neither generates the other.

# SDL2 is a third-party binary distribution copied in from the
# waverace project. The headers and libs are not ours to commit.
src/third_party/SDL/

# The journey has a home so it stops leaking into docs/ - rule 10.2.
# Nothing in it is tracked except the file that says what it is for.
notes/*
!notes/README.txt
